Language English
Debug Off //"{var:EventGalleryExpr11Temp} / {var:EventGalleryExpr12Temp}"

Book Gallery Ordered No Keep Looped

	Page PlaceGallery
		Triggered By @ExploreGalleryViaHall1 If Unread
		
		Prolog """
			You approach the door. It has a small brass plaque that reads
			<<Gallery.>> The door handle catches your eye because light is
			glinting off it. Unlike almost everything else here, it is clean...
			like it has been used recently.
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Add TileGallery
		Remove TokenExploreGalleryViaHall1
		
		Text """
			As the door opens, dust rises then floats with a slow churn.
			Lots of dust. <i>This place could take days to clean,</i> you mumble
			to yourself.
			
			The room behind the door is--or was--stately, with high ceilings,
			beautiful paintings, and furniture and rugs that look both rich and
			comfortable, but now faded and moth-eaten. Dim light from the windows
			reflects off the dust, making the room feel even shabbier.
			
			Place the {c:TileGallery} tile, then discard this Explore token.
		"""
	End Page PlaceGallery
	
	Page PlaceHall2
		Add TokenExploreGalleryViaHall1Sight!, TokenHall1Investigators
		
		Text """
			Feeble light oozes from the {c:TileGallery} into the hallway. 
			Your eyes follow the light to see that the hallway continues into 
			the dark. Place a Sight token as indicated, then move 1 space
			farther down the hall.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenHall1Investigators
		
		Trigger @ExploreHall2ViaHall1
	End Page PlaceHall2
	
	Page PlaceHall1Painting
		Add TokenSearchHall1Painting!

		Text """
			Somehow, light from the {c:TileGallery} has cast a ray directly
			onto a painting next to you, making it glow unnaturally.
			You can feel it calling to you. Unsettled, you shake it off. Place
			a Search token as indicated.
			
			As you look away, something moves in your 
			peripheral vision. You glance back and there is nothing there.
			Except the painting that still glows, seeming more sinister now.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page PlaceHall1Painting
	
	Page ExploreGalleryViaHall1After No Text
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreGalleryViaHall1 If PlaceGallery Is Read And foundSarah
		
		exploredGalleryViaHall1 = true
	End Page ExploreGalleryViaHall1After

	Page ExploreGalleryViaHall1NoSarah
		Not Visible
		Triggered by @ExploreGalleryViaHall1 If PlaceGallery Is Read And Not foundSarahsPainting
		
		Text """
			As you approach the door, your eye is drawn back to the painting
			behind you. Something about it won't let you look away.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page ExploreGalleryViaHall1NoSarah

	Page ExploreGalleryViaHall1NoSarah2
		Not Visible
		Triggered by @ExploreGalleryViaHall1 If PlaceGallery Is Read And foundSarahsPainting And Not foundSarah
		
		Text """
			No matter how hard you try to look away, the girl's quiet glow
			doesn't allow you to.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page ExploreGalleryViaHall1NoSarah2
	
	Page ExploreGalleryViaFoyer No Text
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreGalleryViaFoyer
		
		exploredGalleryViaFoyer = true
	End Page
	
	Page ExploreGalleryAfter
		Prolog """
			You turn back to the {c:TileGallery}. An investigator in the Sight
			token's space can look through the gallery door.
		"""
		Button "Reveal"
		Free

		Text """
			The gallery is larger than it first looked. The ceiling is vaulted
			and windows rise from floor to ceiling. Thick curtains cover the
			windows but one panel has torn. It sags, allowing light into the
			room. Dust continues to catch and scatter it. 
			
			Discard all Sight and Explore tokens leading to this explored area.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenExploreGalleryViaFoyer

		exploredGalleryViaHall1 = true
		exploredGallery = true
	End Page ExploreGalleryAfter
	
	Page PlaceExploreFoyerViaGallery
		Not Visible If exploredFoyer
		
		Remove TokenExploreGalleryViaFoyer
		Add TokenExploreFoyerViaGallery!

		Text """
			Across the room is another door. Place an Explore token as
			indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceExploreFoyerViaGallery

	Page PlaceGalleryCoatRoom
		Add TokenExploreCoatRoomViaGallery!

		Text """
			A coat room sits in the corner across from you, its door ajar.
			Place an Explore token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceGalleryCoatRoom
		
	Page PlaceGalleryDvm
		Add TokenSearchGalleryDvm!

		Text """
			Two divans are upholstered with once-beautiful cloth... but now
			they are moth-eaten and dirty. A pile of junk sits on a small table
			between them. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		Exit
	End Page PlaceGalleryDvm

	Page PlaceCoatRoom
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreCoatRoomViaGallery
		
		Add TokenSearchCoatRoomEvidence!

		Prolog """
			You walk over to the coat room to have a look.
		"""
		Button "Explore"

		Text """
			The coat room still has a number of coats hung neatly on one side.
			Shoes and hangers are scattered on the floor. Discard this Explore
			token.

			A half-filled box sits in one of the corners. Place a Search token
			as indicated.
		"""

		Remove TokenExploreCoatRoomViaGallery
		
		Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		Exit
	End Page PlaceCoatRoom

	Page SearchDvm
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchGalleryDvm
		
		Prolog "A pile of junk sits on the table between the divans."
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchGalleryDvm

		Text QItemDvm """
			Among the tools, handkerchiefs, and ashtrays are a number of small
			books. One of them... <i>feels</i> different than the others. It is
			old and worn, but you get the sense it possesses great power.

			Gain the {c:QItemDvm} Common Item, then discard this Search token.
			This card cannot be removed from the game; if you are asked to,
			drop it instead.
			
			An investigator with the {c:QItemDvm} can interact with it in the
			app.
		"""
		
		foundDvm = true
		Exit
	End Page SearchDvm
	
	Page SearchCoatRoomEvidence
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchCoatRoomEvidence
		
		Prolog """
			This box is half-full of things you might find in a coat room:
			brushes, shoe polish, and...
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchCoatRoomEvidence

		Text QItemEvidenceCoatRoom """
			Among other items, you find a pair of shoes caked with mud and a
			bloody handkerchief. Looking closer, you see that the handkerchief
			was used to wipe blood from the shoes.

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceCoatRoom} Unique Item, then discard this
			Search token.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page SearchCoatRoomEvidence
End Book Gallery